.TH DRAGONGL_CLIENT 1 "@DRAGONGL_RELEASE_DATE@" "Dragon GL @DRAGONGL_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl_client \- Dragon GL 3D game client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl_client
[\fB\-\-fingerprint\fR \fIsha256\fR] [\fB\-\-ui\-scale\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fB\-\-frames\fR \fIn\fR] [\fIserver_host\fR [\fIport\fR]]
.br
.B dragongl_client \-\-print\-config
.br
.B dragongl_client
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help " | " \-V " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl_client
is the 3D client of the Dragon GL dungeon crawler. It connects to a
.BR dragongl_server ,
lets the player create or load a character, and renders the dungeon in
real time with a graphical HUD (stats, minimap, equipment, boss trophies,
compass).

Unless
.I server_host
is given on the command line, the client asks for the server host
(default 127.0.0.1), then for the server password and the player
credentials (passwords are read without echo); new players then choose
race, class and alignment.

The map is received from the server in chunks: the client generates no
local world.
.SS Rendering
The client renders with Vulkan 1.3 and dynamic rendering. The scene is
GPU-driven: compute shaders cull the tile and entity instances around the
player and generate their geometry, and a single indirect draw renders
it. It needs a GPU whose driver supports Vulkan 1.3 with a queue family
for graphics, compute and presentation to the window. At start-up the
client lists the GPUs it found and the one it uses (discrete before
integrated before software, then the most device memory).

The window opens at 80% of the screen and can be resized freely; the
swapchain is rebuilt on resize and whenever the driver reports it out of
date. Closing the window or pressing Escape quits.

When the driver reports the device or the surface lost (a driver update or
reset, a GPU removed), the client rebuilds the renderer on the same window
and the game goes on; after three losses in one session it exits with the
reason. At exit it prints how many frames it drew and their times (median,
99th percentile, maximum).
.SS Window and keys
The HUD shows the character (hit points as a bar and as numbers, vitality,
experience, gold, armour class, abilities, spell slots, conditions), the
minimap, the equipment, the boss trophies and the last messages of the
server. Its size follows the monitor scale and the height of the window;
.B Ctrl+=
and
.B Ctrl+\-
change it.

Commands are typed in the window:
.B Enter
or
.B /
opens the command line,
.B Enter
sends it,
.B Escape
cancels it. While typing: Left, Right, Home, End, Ctrl+Left and Ctrl+Right
(by word), Backspace, Delete, Ctrl+U and Ctrl+K (delete to the start or to
the end), Up and Down (the last 64 commands). Commands may also be typed
in the terminal that started the client, where every message of the server
is printed as well.

Default keys:
.BR W ", " A ", " S ", " D
or the arrows move;
.BR Q " and " E
turn the camera,
.BR R " and " F
raise and lower it,
.BR PageUp " and " PageDown
zoom (the mouse does the same: drag and wheel);
.BR Shift+PageUp " and " Shift+PageDown
scroll the messages;
.B Tab
shows or hides equipment and trophies (hidden by default in a narrow
window);
.B F3
shows the frame time;
.B F1
lists the keys in use;
.B Escape
quits.
.SS Settings file
.I client.conf
(see FILES) holds one setting per line,
.IR "name = value" ;
.B #
starts a comment. A line that is not understood is reported with its
number and the others apply.
.TP
.BR ui_scale " = " auto " | " \fIn\fR
Size of the HUD, 0.5 to 4.
.TP
.BR reduce_motion " = " yes " | " no
No particle effects, combat numbers stay where they appear, the water does
not wave.
.TP
.BR show_fps " = " yes " | " no
Frame time in the top right corner.
.TP
.BI key. action " = " "key\fR[\fB, \fIkey\fR]"
The keys of an action (two at most, or
.BR none ).
A key is a letter, a digit, F1 to F25, a name (Enter, Escape, Tab, Space,
Up, PageUp, KPAdd, Slash, Equal, ...) with optional
.BR Shift+ ", " Ctrl+ ", " Alt+ .
.B \-\-print\-config
lists every action with its default keys.
.TP
.BI bind. key " = " command
The key sends the command as if typed (32 at most), for example
.BR "bind.F5 = look" .
.SS Disconnection
When the server closes the connection, stops answering (TCP keepalive,
about 90 s) or sends a message the client cannot decode, the client prints
the reason and exits. Server and client must speak the same protocol
version.
.SS Server identity
The connection is TLS 1.3. Before it sends the login, the client accepts
the server when its certificate has the fingerprint given with
.BR \-\-fingerprint ,
when an authority the system trusts signed it for
.IR server_host ,
or when
.I known_servers
(below) records that fingerprint for the host and port. At the first
connection to a server with a self-signed certificate the client prints
its fingerprint and records it: compare it with the one the server owner
gives you (the server logs it at start-up). From then on a different
certificate is refused with a warning that names the line to remove if the
owner confirms the change.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I server_host
Host name, IPv4 or IPv6 address of the game server (every address the
name resolves to is tried, 5 s each).
.TP
.I port
TCP port of the game server (default 8080).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-fingerprint " sha256"
Trust only the server certificate with this SHA-256 fingerprint
(\fBSHA256:AB:CD:...\fR, or 64 hexadecimal digits) and record it in
.IR known_servers ,
replacing an older entry for that server.
.TP
.BI \-\-ui\-scale " n"
Size of the HUD, 0.5 to 4; overrides
.B ui_scale
of the settings file.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Write the settings file with every default and key to standard output and
exit. Redirect it to
.I client.conf
and edit it.
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " n"
Draw
.I n
frames, print the frame times and exit (for measurements and tests).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the player quits or the server closes the connection; 1 when the
connection, the login or the renderer fails; 2 for a wrong command line.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_WINDOW
Initial window size as
.IR width x height ,
e.g. 1920x1080.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_GPU
Use this GPU: its index in the start-up list, or part of its name.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_VSYNC
Set to 0 to present without waiting for vertical sync (mailbox or
immediate mode, if the driver offers one).
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_SHADER_DIR
Directory of the compiled shaders. By default they are read from
.I shaders/
next to the executable (build tree), then from
.IR @DRAGONGL_PKGDATADIR@/shaders .
.TP
.B VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS
Vulkan layers to enable, colon separated (for example
.BR VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation );
names the system does not provide are skipped with a warning.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @DRAGONGL_PKGDATADIR@/shaders/*.spv
Compiled shaders.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dragongl/client.conf
Settings and keys
.RI ( ~/.config/dragongl/client.conf
without
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME );
optional.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dragongl/known_servers
Servers trusted by fingerprint
.RI ( ~/.config/dragongl/known_servers
without
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ):
one line per server, \fIhost port sha256\fR, created with mode 0600.
Remove a line to accept a new certificate of that server.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl-client (1),
.BR dragongl_server (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Taibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com>
